<h2>What should I do with an unexpected result?</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Check the sample type, units, collection time and the reference range printed on the report.</li>
  <li>Ask the doctor who ordered the test how your symptoms, medicines and the test method affect the result.</li>
  <li>Ask whether you need a follow-up test. A result flagged outside the range is not a diagnosis by itself.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Can Cortisol+ tell me whether my level is normal?</h2>
<p><strong>No.</strong> Cortisol+ shows wearable stress and recovery signals and a wellness score. It can't tell whether your blood, saliva or urine cortisol is normal.</p>
<p>Never put a 0–100 app score into a lab chart.</p>
<p>Read our <a href="/how-it-works/">methodology and limits</a>, <a href="/stress/apple-watch/">Apple Watch guide</a> and <a href="/cortisol/test/">testing guide</a>.</p>
